   "ruling": "Ruling: scope; Pub. 501 p. 6, Spouse died during the year: \"If your spouse died during the year, you are considered married for the whole year for filing status purposes.\" A head of household filer whose spouse died in 2025 is refused: household.widowed_this_year (hoh branch, household.spouse_died_this_year_if_ever_married) refuses Form 1040 line 12e (forms/2025/f1040.yaml, \"Filing status after a spouse's death in 2025\"), and household.considered_unmarried tells the filer \"if your spouse died in 2025, you are considered married for the whole year: answer No\". So hoh_eligible never decides a completed return for a filer widowed in 2025; the line itself states i1040gi p. 14 correctly. Project stands.",
